# SYNOPSIS

```usage
rm [-fr] file ...
```

# DESCRIPTION

`rm` removes each <file>.
A directory is removed only if it is empty, unless `-r` is given.

: `-f`
  Say nothing of a <file> that can't be removed.
: `-r`
  Remove a directory and everything in it, its files and then its directories, depth first.

# SEE ALSO

mkdir(1), mv(1)

# DIAGNOSTICS

The exit string is the last error, such as `directory not empty`, or empty if each <file> was removed; with `-f`, it is always empty.
